      "id": "s1",
      "nodeId": "n3",
      "text": "Sign up for our email newsletter for the latest science news Sign Up You've likely heard this wild (and wildly misinformed) idea in one form or another: we humans only use 10 percent of our brain.",
      "contextBefore": "equently writes for*Discover Magazine*, covering scientific studies on topics like neuroscience, insects, and microbes. ViewFull Profile. --- Learn about ourEditorial Policy. | 3 min read Newsletter. ",
      "contextAfter": " Like a horror movie monster, the myth just won't die. Various scientists and science journalists think they've killed it. But as soon as they start to relax, it comes roaring back. The fact is, this ",
      "start": 541,
      "end": 737,
      "extractSha256": "84aab4d4b619841df144379f978db93f8ef6a7f62e3956199813edd00dddaa41",
      "windowSha256": "14bdb62c1dbfb4ae8079fe6dbb23d41dfcfa081614d1e9e0ae96803e0a43053a",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-17T23:04:50.484Z",
      "waybackUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/20210909232934/https://www.discovermagazine.com/mind/the-10-percent-of-your-brain-myth-that-just-wont-die",
      "tier": "exact"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "nodeId": "n4",
      "text": "Nearly two-thirds of Americans mistakenly believe that humans use only 10 percent of their brains, according to a new poll on brain health.",
      "contextBefore": " myths and misperceptions abound, including a considerable underestimation of the incidence of brain ailments.\" Busted! Most in US Believe Brain Disease Myths http://www.livescience.com/39923-amer... ",
      "contextAfter": " Do People Only Use 10 Percent Of Their Brains? http://www.scientificamerican.com/art... \"The human brain is complex. Along with performing millions of mundane acts, it composes concertos, issues mani",
      "start": 888,
      "end": 1027,
      "extractSha256": "218c9e432e63340e95b9d6a62b6e2aac6014ecc85985eb77e48feea53ada4749",
      "windowSha256": "13fea5de84172f67a55ffa2768752a6af4f6b91487ebb2ebbb5642ad6fe73df2",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-17T23:04:54.512Z",
      "waybackUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/20130928072756/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JDF2rjFd8hY",
      "tier": "exact"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "nodeId": "n5",
      "text": "In the trailer for the upcoming film *Lucy*, the actor who has played both the President and God addresses an auditorium of students and says, \"It is estimated most human beings only use 10 percent of their brain's capacity...Imagine if we could access 100 percent.\"",
      "contextBefore": "es + Tools & Techniques + See All Blog Lucy and the 10 Percent Brain Myth. * Published16 Jul 2014 * Source The Dana Foundation It's unfair to have Morgan Freeman, with his smooth, deep voice, say it. ",
      "contextAfter": " It's hard not to believe Morgan Freeman. But in this case, he's wrong. The idea that we only use 10 percent of our brains is a myth. \"The crazy thing about this belief is that despite being totally f",
